&lt;p&gt;Canonical builds the open-source software that runs the world’s clouds, devices and AI, and we hold our managers to a high standard. Our Talent Development team exists to make leaders and managers at Canonical genuinely excellent. We define what great management looks like here, and we bring managers and leaders up to that standard through direct, hands-on work, both from the centre and embedded inside engineering and commercial organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Organisational Development Practitioner you are the person who sets the bar for how coaching and organisational development is practised here. You coach leaders to a clear standard of management excellence. You diagnose how a whole organisation is led and drive the plan to raise it. You develop the practitioners working in the field. It is one of the most senior and demanding Talent roles at Canonical: hands-on coaching and organisational-development craft with real leaders, in a company that expects you to be credible in a room of directors and to earn that credibility fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You work both from the central team and embedded inside a leader&#39;s organisation for periods, turning what you learn in the field back into how we develop leaders and managers across Canonical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: These are remote based positions, available across EMEA and the Americas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you deliver&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
